REBUILDING WORKERS
------------------

- Download and install "Rust" from https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install. 
  Use the recommended "rustup". Select the 64-bit installer.

  It will include the Rust compiler and Cargo package manager. 
  To check, run from command line:

    > rustc --version
    > cargo --version

  To update Rust:

    > rustup update

- Go to the worker's folder.

- If required, adjust the versions in "Cargo.toml" file, "[dependencies]" section.
  
  To check for updates:

    > cargo update --verbose

- To build:

    > cargo build --release

  Or start "build.cmd", if exists.

  It will generate the "target\release\XXXWorker.exe".

- Rebuild ("Rebuild All") the Visual Studio solution. A Custom build step 
  will copy 'XXXWorker.exe' to output folder as 'XXXWorker.bin'.

- Commit and push the changes to Git (including 'XXXWorker.exe'). 


MAKING NEW WORKERS
------------------

- Create a new subfolder, enter it.

- Execute:

    > cargo init --verbose

- To reference crates ("json", for example):

    > cargo add json --verbose

- Add ".gitignore" (from other workers). Typically:

Cargo.lock
!target/**
target/*.*
target/release/*
!target/release/*.exe
target/debug/*
target/flycheck0/*

- Build worker as explained above.
